# The reduction and analysis tooling is executed by bash inside WSL. With
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows, git rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout and
# WSL's bash then fails on the stray \r -- silently enough that a driver script
# can appear to "run" and produce nothing (see LESSONS.md, ops).
#
# Default everything to LF. Attributes beat core.autocrlf and travel with the repo,
# so any clone on any machine is runnable -- which a local git config would not give.
# Data files need this as much as scripts: a URL list with CRLF fetches fine and then
# fails every filename check built from the same string (LESSONS.md, M29).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The executable text, called out because these are the ones that fail silently.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sof  text eol=lf

# Binary -- never rewritten. Listed explicitly rather than left to content sniffing.
*.npz  binary
*.png  binary

# M37 freezes these audited upstream artifacts byte-for-byte. Their source whitespace is
# hash-bound in data/repro/manifest.json and must not be normalized merely to satisfy a diff
# diagnostic.
data/repro/viper/results/* -whitespace
data/repro/viper/viper-tracked.patch -whitespace

# Release source archives omit third-party full text and unsent correspondence.
# These remain in Git history; this is an archive-content rule, not a history rewrite.
papers/text export-ignore
papers/text/** export-ignore
docs/paper/author-query-draft.md export-ignore
